body:
If I want to override the `active` or `inactive` templates of the `showMore` in a `refinementList`, it seems that I have to override both.

If I only supply `options.showMore.templates.active` or `options.showMore.templates.inactive`, then I'm greeted with `Uncaught Error: Template must be 'string' or 'function', was 'undefined' (key: show-more-inactive)`.

The workaround is to provide both templates, but the ideal fix would be to allow overriding only one of the two, and use the default value for the other one.

```javascript
instantsearch.widgets.refinementList({
  showMore: {
    templates: {
      active: 'this will fail'
      // inactive:'unless this is uncommented',
    }
  }
})
```
